   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Two tenses, two stories",
     "texto": [
      "The perfect (**cheguei**, I arrived) presents a completed past action; the imperfect (**chovia**, it was raining) can present a background situation, a habit or an action in progress.",
      "Example: **Quando cheguei, chovia** (when I arrived, it was raining). The arrival happens during a situation that was already under way."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "«Enquanto» and «quando»",
     "texto": [
      "**Enquanto** (while) usually joins simultaneous actions: **Enquanto eu lia, ela dormia** (while I was reading, she was sleeping).",
      "**Quando** means «when»; it does not decide the tense by itself. Context and meaning determine the tense: **Quando chegaste, eu comia** (when you arrived, I was eating), **Quando chegaste, comecei a cozinhar** (when you arrived, I started cooking)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
